{
  "_comment": "EMR Lake Formation FGAC expected-support matrix. THIS IS REAL DATA transcribed from AWS documentation, not synthetic. It is the 'expected state' the comparison engine diffs observed results against, so that a documented 'Not supported' is reported as EXPECTED_UNSUPPORTED instead of a false regression.",
  "sources": [
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-lf-fgac1.html",
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/EMR-Serverless-UserGuide/emr-serverless-lf-enable.html",
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/EMR-Serverless-UserGuide/lake-formation-unfiltered-access.html"
  ],
  "retrieved": "2026-08-13",
  "access_mode": "lf_fgac",
  "state_codes": {
    "S": "SUPPORTED \u2014 uses Lake Formation credentials exclusively; no fallback to runtime-role credentials if LF permissions are insufficient",
    "S3": "SUPPORTED_WITH_S3_IAM \u2014 does NOT use LF credentials; runtime role needs direct S3 IAM on the table location regardless of registration",
    "N": "NOT_SUPPORTED \u2014 documented as unsupported; a failure here is expected behavior, not a regression"
  },
  "version_gates": {
    "fgac_min_release": "6.15.0",
    "fgac_min_release_emr_serverless": "7.2.0",
    "fgac_min_release_emr_on_eks": "7.7.0",
    "dml_ddl_use_lf_credentials_from": "7.12.0",
    "dml_ddl_use_runtime_role_credentials_before": "7.12.0",
    "delete_update_merge_unsupported_at_or_before": "7.11.0",
    "recordserver_sql_extension_required_before": "7.10.0",
    "notes": [
      "7.12: DML and DDL operations that modify table data switch from runtime-role credentials to Lake Formation vended credentials. Highest-risk documented upgrade change: the identity that writes your data changes.",
      "7.11 and older: DELETE, UPDATE and MERGE are not supported under FGAC at all.",
      "Before 7.10: Delta and Hudi require com.amazonaws.emr.recordserver.connector.spark.sql.RecordServerSQLExtension in spark.sql.extensions and spark_catalog.lf.managed=true. Iceberg catalog impl changes from SparkCatalog to SparkSessionCatalog. The customer's Spark conf must change across the upgrade.",
      "The 7.12.0 boundary is the documented point at which DML and DDL switch from runtime-role credentials to Lake Formation vended credentials, and at which DELETE/UPDATE/MERGE become supported. Verify against the current AWS documentation for your release."
    ]
  },
  "lf_permission_map_summary": {
    "DESCRIBE": "read table or database metadata in the Data Catalog",
    "ALTER": "modify table or database metadata in the Data Catalog",
    "DROP": "delete table or database metadata from the Data Catalog",
    "SELECT": "read table data from Amazon S3",
    "INSERT": "write table data to Amazon S3",
    "DELETE": "delete table data from Amazon S3",
    "evaluation": "Lake Formation evaluates permissions lazily when Spark calls Glue for metadata or S3 for data. A job with insufficient permissions does not fail until the call that needs the missing permission is made."
  },
